## Layer 1: Structure Array Mapping (Bug Fix)

### Scope Contract
Fix the critical Sanity UI crash `List items must be of type "listItem", got "object"`. The root `items()` array in Sanity's `.list()` expects `ListItemBuilder` elements, but the previous agent passed a `DocumentListBuilder` direct reference.

### DoD

- [ ] 1.1 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: In the main `structure` export list (around line 38), change `buildCatalogueTree(S),` to `S.listItem().title("Catalogue").child(buildCatalogueTree(S)),`. Wrap the builder dynamically.
  - Difficulty: 1 - B(sanity/structure.ts): wrap root list item to resolve crash

### Verification — Layer 1

- [ ] V1.1 — Open Sanity Studio at `http://localhost:3000/studio`. Confirm the Studio loads properly without the red error screen, and the "Catalogue" folder is visible.
  - Difficulty: 1

