## Layer 2: Context-Aware Document Creation

### Scope Contract
The previous sprint registered the `catalogueItem-with-parent` initial value template in `sanity.config.ts`, but failed to actually bind it to the dynamic structure list. We must tell Sanity to use this specific template (and pass it the `parentId`) when an editor clicks the "+" button while viewing a specific nested folder.

### DoD

- [ ] 2.1 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: Update the `buildCatalogueTree` function. Chain the `.initialValueTemplates` method onto `S.documentTypeList("catalogueItem")` dynamically based on whether `parentId` is present.
  If a `parentId` is defined, call `.initialValueTemplates([ S.initialValueTemplateItem("catalogueItem-with-parent", { parentId }) ])`.
  If no `parentId` is defined (root level), do not chain `.initialValueTemplates` (letting Sanity use the default root document creation).
  - Difficulty: 3 - A(sanity/structure.ts): bind templates to contextual tree lists

### Verification — Layer 2

- [ ] V2.1 — Open Studio > Catalogue. Click a root item like "Headphones" > "View Sub-Items". Click the pencil/plus icon at the top to create a new sub-item. Ensure the right-side creation pane has the "Parent Item" reference field PRE-FILLED with "Headphones" automatically.
  - Difficulty: 2

